\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Absolutely. The coordination problem is actually the heart of what you\'92re describing.\
If 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Script.god
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  is standalone, I would define its job very narrowly and powerfully:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf2 \strokec2 Script.god coordinates information, tasks, state, and communication between independent models.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
It should not try to become the models. It should be the layer that makes separate models behave like one coordinated system.\
Imagine LMLM has five independent models:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2                  Script.god\
                      \uc0\u9474 \
        \uc0\u9484 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9488 \
        \uc0\u9474              \u9474              \u9474 \
     Model A       Model B       Model C\
     Reasoning      Coding        Vision\
        \uc0\u9474              \u9474              \u9474 \
        \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9496 \
                      \uc0\u9474 \
                  Model D\
                  Research\
                      \uc0\u9474 \
                  Model E\
                  Planning\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 Without coordination, every model has its own context, state, knowledge, and objectives.\
With Script.god:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2                  Shared Coordination\
                         \uc0\u9474 \
        \uc0\u9484 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9488 \
        \uc0\u9660                 \u9660                 \u9660 \
    Information        Tasks             State\
        \uc0\u9474                 \u9474                 \u9474 \
        \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9496 \
                         \uc0\u9660 \
                    All Models\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 There are four coordination problems Script.god should solve.\
First: information coordination.\
If Model D discovers something new, Script.god can determine whether that information matters to the other models.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Research Model\
      \uc0\u9474 \
      \uc0\u9474  discovers information\
      \uc0\u9660 \
 Script.god\
      \uc0\u9474 \
      \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  verify\
      \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  classify\
      \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  version\
      \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472  determine relevance\
             \uc0\u9474 \
       \uc0\u9484 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9488 \
       \uc0\u9660      \u9660      \u9660 \
     Code  Vision  Planning\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 Second: task coordination.\
Instead of sending the same task to every model, Script.god decomposes it.\
For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 USER:\
Build a new AI application.\
\
Script.god:\
\
Planner \uc0\u8594  architecture\
Researcher \uc0\u8594  investigate technologies\
Coder \uc0\u8594  implementation\
Tester \uc0\u8594  testing\
Security \uc0\u8594  security analysis\
Documentation \uc0\u8594  documentation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 Then Script.god combines their outputs.\
Third: state coordination.\
This is extremely important.\
A model might know:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 project.version = 1.4\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 while another thinks:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 project.version = 1.3\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 Script.god should maintain the authoritative state:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Canonical State\
version = 1.4\
status = tested\
deployment = staging\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 Models don\'92t independently decide the global state.\
They report to the coordinator.\
Fourth: dependency coordination.\
Suppose the research model changes a technical assumption.\
Script.god should identify which other models are affected.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Research change\
      \uc0\u8595 \
Dependency graph\
      \uc0\u8595 \
\uc0\u9484 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9488 \
\uc0\u9660      \u9660       \u9660 \
Code  Tests  Docs\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 That\'92s where the system becomes interesting.\
Script.god could maintain a live coordination graph:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2              \uc0\u9484 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9488 \
             \uc0\u9474  Research  \u9474 \
             \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9516 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9496 \
                   \uc0\u9474 \
             new information\
                   \uc0\u9474 \
                   \uc0\u9660 \
             \uc0\u9484 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9488 \
             \uc0\u9474  Script.god\u9474 \
             \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9516 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9496 \
                   \uc0\u9474 \
       \uc0\u9484 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9488 \
       \uc0\u9660            \u9660            \u9660 \
    Planning     Coding     Security\
       \uc0\u9474            \u9474            \u9474 \
       \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9496 \
                   \uc0\u9660 \
                Testing\
                   \uc0\u9474 \
                   \uc0\u9660 \
              Verification\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 I\'92d also distinguish between 
\f2\b \cf2 \strokec2 broadcasting
\f0\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  and 
\f2\b \cf2 \strokec2 coordination
\f0\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 .\
Broadcasting is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Information \uc0\u8594  everyone\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 Coordination is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Information\
     \uc0\u8595 \
Script.god\
     \uc0\u8595 \
Who needs it?\
     \uc0\u8595 \
What do they need?\
     \uc0\u8595 \
When do they need it?\
     \uc0\u8595 \
What should they do with it?\
     \uc0\u8595 \
What depends on their response?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 That difference is crucial.\
For example, if a new CUDA API is discovered, a vision model probably doesn\'92t need the entire technical document. The coding model might need the API specification, the testing model might need compatibility information, and the documentation model might need a summarized change.\
Script.god should therefore transform information according to the receiving model.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2                  New Information\
                       \uc0\u9474 \
                 Script.god\
                       \uc0\u9474 \
          \uc0\u9484 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9532 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9488 \
          \uc0\u9660             \u9660             \u9660 \
       Coding        Testing     Documentation\
          \uc0\u9474             \u9474             \u9474 \
       Full API      Changes      Summary\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 That means Script.god isn\'92t just an information pipe.\
It\'92s an 
\f2\b \cf2 \strokec2 information coordinator
\f0\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 .\
The other major feature I\'92d introduce is a coordination ID.\
Every piece of work gets an identity:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 coordination_id = "LMLM-2026-0814-00042"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 Everything associated with that operation carries the ID:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Task\
Information\
Model responses\
Decisions\
Errors\
Verification\
State changes\
Artifacts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 So Script.god can reconstruct exactly what happened.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Coordination\
   \uc0\u9474 \
   \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  Task\
   \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  Research\
   \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  Model A\
   \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  Model B\
   \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  Model C\
   \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  Decision\
   \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472  Verification\
   \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472  Final state\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 This gives you traceability.\
And I would make coordination 
\f2\b \cf2 \strokec2 bidirectional
\f0\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 .\
Not:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Script.god \uc0\u8594  Models\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 but:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2               Script.god\
             \uc0\u8601     \u8595     \u8600 \
          Model  Model  Model\
             \uc0\u8598     \u8593     \u8599 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 Models can report:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 completed\
failed\
uncertain\
conflict\
new_information\
requires_help\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Coding Model:\
"I found a conflict with the current dependency."\
\
        \uc0\u8595 \
\
Script.god:\
\
pause dependent tasks\
notify research model\
request resolution\
update state\
resume affected tasks\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 That gives the system something resembling a distributed nervous system.\
The standalone 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 Script.god
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  doesn\'92t need to own every model. It simply coordinates them through standardized messages.\
I would ultimately make its coordination model:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf2 \strokec2 Discover \uc0\u8594  Assign \u8594  Communicate \u8594  Share \u8594  Observe \u8594  Resolve \u8594  Verify \u8594  Synchronize \u8594  Continue.
\f0\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
That is the foundation I\'92d use for Script.god before worrying about syntax or implementation.\
